FunctieVivaldis Office is looking for a Customer Service Officer for our client in Hasselt. Our client is specialised in incident management and roadside assistance.Feel free to take a look at the vacancy! If you have any questions, you can reach us by phone on  3211 94 81 56.Your duties as a customer service officer will include:
• You'll respond to incoming phone calls and mails;
• You'll gather the necessary information and check it's accuracy and completeness;
• You'll provide the needed technical support and communicate with the workshops;
• You'll update all the involved parties;
• You'll monitor the agreements;
• You'll follow the contract-related issues up and respect the imposed deadlines.Profiel
As a customer service officer you can recognise yourself in the criteria below:

• Preferably you have gained a first experience in customer service;
• You can easily work with the computer, especially with MS Office;
• You're a social person with strong communication skills;
• You have attention to detail and are stress-resistant;
• You work organised and have great organizational and time management skills;
• You must speak fluently Dutch/Polish/English OR Polish/ German/ English OR English/German/Dutch OR French/ German/ English
• You work the weekend   Friday shift OR during the week. You work 40 hours/ week between 07.00-22.00h.Wat je van ons krijgt
What's in it for you as the new customer service officer:

• You'll end up in a leading company in an international environment;
• You'll work in a full-time position with a strong emphasis on work-life balance;
• You'll receive a competitive salary including meal vouchers worth €7 and eco-vouchers;
• The company hosts various social events to boost the team spirit;
• Hard work pays off! After a successful interim period you'll receive a permanent contract.
We look forward to your application if you're convinced of this vacancy.

.

An international organisation located in Brussels working in the investment field. 

Jobomschrijving

We are looking for a dynamic Assistant to work in the heart of Brussels! 

Your responsibilities are the following; 

• Welcome and direct visitors, manage logistics before, during and after visits (organising schedules, welcoming visitors, preparing and cleaning meeting rooms, organising catering, setting up equipment, etc.);
• Manage incoming/outgoing standard and express mail and parcels (reception, encoding, distribution, dispatch);
• Clean and organise office environment;
• Prepare agendas and schedules for meetings;
• Book taxis, restaurants and co-working spaces;
• Help organise and prepare small internal events;
• Logistical and practical organisation and coordination of domestic and international travels;
• Administrative welcome for new employees;
• Other related duties as assigned;
• Back-up in case of absence of other assistants;
• Team support when needed to accomplish results.

Which profile are we looking for? 

• High school diploma or equivalent experience (at least 1 year); 
• Perfect knowledge of Dutch and English; knowledge of French is an asset 
• Excellent knowledge of the Office suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and collaborative tools (Outlook, network, etc.);
• Dynamic, flexible, ability to work independently as well as in a team;
• Helpful, team player, solution oriented;
• Ability to multitask, meet changing deadlines;
• Excellent organisational skills and attention to details.

Our client is an international public affairs agency located in Brussels. 

Jobomschrijving

Do you have experience in working as an Office Manager in an international environment? Are you fluent in French and English? We have the right job for you! 

We are looking for an Office Manager (m/f/x) for one of our clients in Brussels. 

As Office Manager (m/f/x), you would be responsible for:

Perform administrative tasks for the office, e.g. relations with suppliers, organisation of office meetings and client visits;

Assist with onboarding of new staff;

Manage holiday plans and absences;

Contribute to website and social media channels;

Create content for clients’ websites and social media channels;

Handle invoices;

Liaise with external accountants to process invoices;

Produce expenditure reports;

Prepare content for client meetings, seminars and other events;

Other tasks: Ad-hoc support to client-related activities.

The successful candidate will be an experienced professional who demonstrates the following experiences and competencies:

Relevant degree

At least 2-3 years of working experience in similar positions

Full proficiency (writing and speaking) in English and French (an additional language is an asset);

Very good IT skills (e.g. command of MS Office, incl. in particular Excel, Powerpoint) Desirable

Strong organisational skills

Hard-working and flexible

Eye to detail; result-orientation
